# Go tests

Follow [.cursor/skills/go-tests/SKILL.md](../skills/go-tests/SKILL.md) for full conventions.

- Assert real behavior; no empty or tautological tests.
- Prefer table-driven tests and `t.Run` subtests.
- `t.Helper()` only in helpers — not in top-level tests.
- Per-case `wantOutput` for CLI tests; help → stdout, invalid usage → stderr.
- Inject I/O; use `t.TempDir()` for filesystem tests.
- Unit tests stay local; public CLI/hook end-to-end paths belong in `e2e/`.
